<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="crafting-professions">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c5" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_helmet_goggles_pandariatradeskill_d_01.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Best Professions &amp; Crafted Gear for Shadow Priests</span></h2>Every profession is viable in Mists of Pandaria Classic, all giving similar power benefits in a variety of implementations. Our preferred choice is Engineering, due to the utility of effects and early craftable armor, and Tailoring, due to the multiplicative scaling of the embroidery buffs. Other professions provide values that usually average out to about 320 Intellect in power level, but are overshadowed by our two main choices. Our only lackluster choices are the Gathering professions, as their benefits are minuscule to non-existent. Herbalism is the only one worth mentioning with its Haste buff; however, it is overshadowed by the added Intellect from the other professions.<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="engineering">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c5" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/ui_profession_engineering.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Engineering for Shadow Priests</h4>Engineering brings with it the following:<br/>
<br/>
<a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=126731/synapse-springs">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_engineering.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Synapse Springs</span></a> which you can apply to your Glove slot, giving you a 1920 Intellect buff that lasts for 10 seconds on a 1-minute cooldown. This averages out to about 320 Intellect as long as you use it whenever it is available.<br/>
<br/>
<a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=54793/frag-belt">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_engineering.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Frag Belt</span></a>, which can be applied to the Waist slot, allowing you to deal some damage off the global cooldown occasionally.<br/>
<br/>
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=77533/lightweight-retinal-armor">
<img alt="Lightweight Retinal Armor" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_helmet_goggles_pandariatradeskill_d_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Lightweight Retinal Armor</span></a>, which is a powerful piece of early equipment that you can socket with special Cogwheel Gems, giving a better benefit than regular gems in the early game.<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="tailoring">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c5" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/ui_profession_tailoring.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Tailoring for Shadow Priests</h4>Tailoring gives embroideries that you will definitely get some use out of via <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=125482/darkglow-embroidery">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_thread_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Darkglow Embroidery</span></a> or <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=142173/lightweave-embroidery">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_thread_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Lightweave Embroidery</span></a>. In addition, there are some early game pieces that Tailoring can craft, however, none of them require Tailoring to equip.<div class="pad exclude-units"></div>
<h3 class="heading-size-3 heading-bar" id="crafted-gear">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c5" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_chest_cloth_challengepriest_d_01.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Best Crafted Gear for Shadow Priests</span></h3>Crafted items are no longer restricted by your Profession option, except for Engineering, so this allows us to equip Tailoring items without Tailoring if we need to.<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=86312/legacy-of-the-emperor">
<img alt="Legacy of the Emperor" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_chest_cloth_challengepriest_d_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Legacy of the Emperor</span></a> is an excellent piece that you'll use when Mogu'shan Vaults is all that is accessible. The materials can be tough to work with, so be on the lookout for a replacement chest piece if you are unable to obtain this one.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=77533/lightweight-retinal-armor">
<img alt="Lightweight Retinal Armor" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_helmet_goggles_pandariatradeskill_d_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Lightweight Retinal Armor</span></a> is a strong Pre-BIS option for Shadow Priests that are obtained through Engineering. They let you take advantage of Cogwheel Sockets to get increased stat bonuses, and as a 476-piece, it has a solid amount of Intellect on it.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=82439/robes-of-creation">
<img alt="Robes of Creation" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_chest_cloth_panda_b_01_red.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Robes of Creation</span></a> is a nice chestpiece that also has a solid amount of Spirit on it, allowing us to use it for Hit itemization.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=82437/spelltwisters-grand-robe">
<img alt="Spelltwister's Grand Robe" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_robe_raidmage_l_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Spelltwister's Grand Robe</span></a> is another chest option that sacrifices Spirit for Haste, which is solid if you don't need Spirit for your Hit itemization.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=82438/spelltwisters-gloves">
<img alt="Spelltwister's Gloves" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_glove_raidmage_l_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Spelltwister's Gloves</span></a> is another solid crafting piece that allows us to get more Hit for our 15% Hit Rating. It is also a 476 piece, so it comes with increased Intellect over Heroic dungeon gear.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=79335/inscribed-red-fan">
<img alt="Inscribed Red Fan" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_offhand_1h_pandariatradeskill_c_02.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Inscribed Red Fan</span></a> is another solid piece from Inscription that will carry you until you can buy the piece from Celestial Dungeons.</div></li></ul>
